      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "Label": "UNLABELLED",
          "content": "This study assessed the value of dobutamine 201Tl scintigraphy for detecting significant disease of infarct-related and remote coronary arteries in myocardial infarction patients."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Dobutamine (up to 40 micrograms/kg/min)/atropine (up to 1 mg) stress test in conjunction with stress-reinjection 200Tl SPECT was performed in 71 symptomatic patients with left ventricular dysfunction > 3 mo after myocardial infarction. Ischemia was defined as reversible perfusion defects."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Significant coronary artery stenosis (> or = 50% luminal diameter stenosis) was detected in all patients. Sensitivity, specificity and accuracy of regional ischemia for the diagnosis of remote coronary artery stenosis were 74% (95% Cl 63-86), 80% (Cl 70-90) and 76% (Cl 65-87), respectively. Those for infarct-related artery stenosis were 71% (Cl 60-81), 83% (Cl 75-92) and 72% (Cl 61-82), respectively. Ischemic perfusion score was higher in patients with multiversus single-vessel disease (1056 +/- 1021 versus 423 +/- 633, p < 0.01)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Dobutamine thallium scintigraphy is valuable for assessing the extent of coronary stenosis on the basis of reversible hypoperfusion in symptomatic patients late after myocardial infarction."
        }
      ]},
